devlog integration for the V0 probe and the V5 hello -- NOT APPLIED (a later step; see vita/devlog/README.md and
vita/notes/devlog.md). Revision-3 wiring, regenerated 2026-10-07 against main at afdb105 (vita/probe/main.c includes
adb0e7a); vita/hello/host.c and vita/probe/main.c only. Both patched files compile warning-free with arm-vita-eabi-gcc
(probe -Wall -Wextra, hello with build.sh's flags).
  apply:  git apply vita/devlog/integrate.patch     (check first: git apply --check vita/devlog/integrate.patch)
No build file changes: each app includes ../devlog/devlog_unity.c (the whole client, static except devlog_*) and
../devlog/devlog_pad.h (the question's X / CIRCLE / START answer); arm-vita-eabi-gcc's default link libraries already
carry the SceNet / SceNetCtl / SceSysmodule stubs, and both apps link SceCtrl already.
Without ux0:data/shepherd/devlog.txt (enabled=1 + token) both apps behave exactly as before: no network, no files.
Both set .defer_launch_send = 1, so no network runs during the probe's measurements or hello's start:
  probe  runs kept from earlier launches go with devlog_end (auto) or the question; devlog_wait(5000) right after
         devlog_begin lets the launch copies finish and the worker (32 KiB stack) go before test_memory measures.
  hello  devlog_send_now(1) once the Mono arena and the Mono thread are in place, only when devlog_begin returned
         DEVLOG_PENDING (mode=auto): in mode=ask a send_now(1) would be a yes the user never gave.
mode=ask: after devlog_end both show the question (devlog_ask_console); the probe only while its debug screen is
visible (not when vitaGL owns the display, vgl=1: the runs stay kept and the next app that asks covers them).
hello reports DEVLOG_PENDING / DEVLOG_REJECTED / an unanswered question in hello.txt.

